# Caddyfile — reverse-proxy the standalone wasm-visor on a subdomain.
#
# `skywire cli hv serve` (the skywire-wasm-visor-serve.service in this directory) serves
# the keyless self-contained page on 127.0.0.1:7999; Caddy fronts it with auto-HTTPS.
# Restart that service after a skywire update to serve the new build (the page is built
# from the running binary's embedded wasm + UI).
#
# Replace wasm.example.net with your subdomain.
#
# SAFETY: the served page is KEYLESS — each visitor's browser mints + persists its own
# ephemeral key (localStorage); the page NEVER asks for a secret key, so serving from a
# domain is safe. (The key-entry-spoof risk only applies to key-BEARING `hv gen` files —
# never serve those from a domain.)

wasm.example.net {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:7999
}
